.venv
.env
logs
tests/runs
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# Runtime-generated per-install state (gitignored too) — a cloud image must boot CLEAN for every
# new tenant/demo session, never with the operator's own personal memory/config baked in. Found
# 2026-07-23 (INI-018 T1): the image was shipping the operator's real memory.db + config/*.json.
memory/_data
widgets/_data/*/
config/*.json
# …EXCEPT the model table (V2-500), which is the opposite kind of file: tracked, public, and READ AT BOOT by
# config/models.py, provider_chain, workers/providers and memory/embeddings. The rule above exists to keep the
# OPERATOR'S per-install json (settings/connectors/v2, all gitignored) out of a tenant image; this one has to be
# in it. Without this line the image builds perfectly and every Machine dies on the first read with
# `FileNotFoundError: config/models.default.json` — `config/models.py` fails loudly on purpose.
!config/models.default.json
.meshkore/credentials
.meshkore/logs
